---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import SampleComponent from "@components/SampleComponent.astro";
import Container from "@components/Container.astro";
import AstroLogo from "@assets/images/astro-logo-light-gradient.png";
import { Content as SampleMarkdown } from "@content/sample-markdown.md";
import Header from "@components/Header.astro"
import HeaderMobile from "@components/HeaderMobile.astro"
import Footer from "@components/Footer.astro"
import LargePin from "@components/largepin.astro"
---

<Layout title="Web Design">
  <Container>

  <Header/>
  <HeaderMobile/>
  <div class="page">

<h1>UI/UX Design</h1>
<div class="content1 project-row">

<div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/chet-large.webp" link="https://thechetshow.com" />
</div>

<div class="text">
  <h2>"The Chet Show" Thesis Site</h2>

<p class="year">(2026)</p>
<p>
Built for SUNY New Paltz’s 2026 Thesis <br><br> 

“The Chet Show” was a rounchy college-comedy short film series that I had created alongside my goodfriend Candice Leach. The project was very fun and had a very high production value.<br><br>For my thesis I decided to document this project through my knowledge of web design simply due to the large scope of the series and how the skills I utilized to manage it all were learnt more from my years of doing design work. In the end <a href="https://thechetshow.com" >thechetshow.com</a> ended up being the largest website I had ever developed up until this point. Utilizing all the content and design skills I had built up until this point, I was able to create a website that acts as a truly memorable user experience.
</p>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="content1 project-row">

<div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/launch-large.webp" link="https://launch.michaellosquadro.com" />
</div>

<div class="text">
  <h2>My Launch Page</h2>

<p class="year">(2025)</p>
<p>
Built for SUNY New Paltz’s Fall 2025 Web Design 2 course.<br><br> This launch page was built to act as a small highway, linking together all of my congruent projects and websites. Going for a very simple aesthetic, this was primarily used as a playground for some javascript functionality.<br><br> Make sure to check out this site on desktop for some fun interactive visuals!
</p>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="content1 project-row">
  <div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/uup-large.webp" link="https://uuphost.org/newpaltzwp" />
  </div> 
  <div class="text">
<h2>New Paltz UUP Website</h2>
<p class="year">(2025)</p>
<p>
Created for SUNY New Paltz’s Fall 2025 Client Design Course.<br><br> I was assigned as an Intern for the UUP’s New Paltz branch. In this role I was tasked to rebuild the New Paltz branch’s wordpress site.<br><br>
By the end of the project I had completely rebuilt the website from the ground up, bringing it into the modern era of wordpress. as well as updating the site to be usable on mobile devices. <br><br>
Some of my favorite aspects I built into the new site was implementing mail chimp implementation and improving the workflow from google calendar to the website, creating a more self-sufficient website that operates more freely with less direct involvement from moderators.
</p>
  </div> </div>

  <div class="content1 project-row">
  <div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/hotw-large.webp" link="https://losquadm1.github.io/historyofweb/" />
  </div>
  <div class="text">
<h2>History of the Web</h2>
<p class="year">(2024)</p>
<p>
Built for SUNY New Paltz’s Spring 2024 Web Design 1 course<br><br>

History of the Web is a guided tour through the internet, hosted by everyone’s favorite artificial personality HostBot! This was the first website I had ever built, a great learning experiece that was very ambitious at the time. The project was recently updated to work on desktop, as it was originally built for mobile devices exclusively. 
</p>
  </div></div>

<div class="content1 project-row">
  <div class="image">
  <LargePin pic="/img/pin/chami-large.webp" link="/ui-ux/chami" />
  </div>
  <div class="text">
<h2>Chami</h2>
<p class="year">(2022)</p>

<p>

Built for SUNY New Paltz’s Fall 2022 Visual Language course<br><br>
Chami is an online messenger app concept created for the 2022 Visual Language course offered at SUNY New Paltz. The project focused around creating a fun and interesting brand as well as some mockups for a few of the app's pages.
</p>
  </div></div>


</div>
  
</div>

  </div>
  <Footer/>

  </Container>
  </Layout>


  <style>
.page{
  flex-direction: column;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center
}

.content1{
display: flex;
flex-direction: row;
flex-wrap: wrap;
padding-top:20px;
justify-content: center;
}

.project-row{
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 600px) minmax(360px, 600px);
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 10px;
}

.project-row .image,
.project-row .text{
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
}

.text{
  max-width:600px;
padding-left:30px;
padding-right:30px; 
}

.text h2{
  margin-bottom: 1px;
  line-height: 1.25;
}

.text .year{
  margin-top: 0;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-size: 0.92em;
}

.text p{
  margin-top: 0;
}


@media (max-width: 768px){
.image{
  padding-left:10px;
  padding-right:10px;
}

.project-row{
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  gap: 0;
}
}


  </style>